### G1 — Zero coherent digits are not covered by the C3 read proof

The proof universally states:

> “A slot with coherent digit \(\Gamma_t\) is represented … as  
> \(M_sg_t,\quad dv_i(g_t)=0,\quad \operatorname{res}(g_t)=\Gamma_t.\)”

But T1 explicitly permits \(c_t=0\), hence \(\Gamma_t=0\). A value-zero factor cannot have zero residue. Therefore this representation and the stated graded scalar-covariance argument do not cover zero slots. The formula may still be true there, but (C3-canonical-read), and consequently the slotwise derivation of (C3-three-reads), has an unproved zero-coefficient branch.

Classification: GAP.

### m1 — The coefficient representatives defining \(L_M\) remain unbound

(C6) says:

> “Define  
> \(L_M(\lambda)=\sum_{r=0}^{f_1-1}\widetilde{\lambda_r}x^{i+e_1r}\pi^{a-rh}.\)”

No residue-section or choice of representatives \(\lambda_r\mapsto\widetilde{\lambda_r}\) is fixed. Thus \(L_M\) is not literally a defined function from the displayed carrier data, although its asserted valuation and residue properties are independent of the usual permissible choice.

Classification: MINOR.

VERDICT: FINDINGS: 0C + 1G + 1m
